{% comment %}
  sections/multicolumn.liquid

  Repeatable content columns — features, steps, services.

  ## What changed in Phase 3

  The old `mobile_layout` select chose between a stacked grid and a carousel by
  rendering two entirely separate wrappers around the same captured blocks. That
  made mobile the only breakpoint with a choice: desktop was always a grid, and
  the two branches had drifted apart on arrows and labelling.

  It is now the shared shell, which means desktop can be a carousel too — a
  reasonable thing to want for eight service columns — and there is one wrapper.

  ## Migration

  `mobile_layout` becomes `layout_mobile`, with the same two values under
  different names ('stack' → 'grid'). The Liquid below translates the old value
  so an installed store keeps its layout without the merchant reopening the
  editor. Remove the fallback a release after the settings have been re-saved.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign layout_mob = section.settings.layout_mobile

  if layout_mob == blank
    assign legacy = section.settings.mobile_layout
    if legacy == 'stack'
      assign layout_mob = 'grid'
    elsif legacy == 'carousel'
      assign layout_mob = 'carousel'
    else
      assign layout_mob = 'grid'
    endif
  endif
-%}

<div
  class="multicolumn color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}"
  {% render 'spacing', section: section.settings %}
>
  <div class="{% render 'container', width: section.settings.container_width %}">
    {%- comment -%}
      The carousel element, written here rather than through
      `snippets/carousel-shell.liquid`.

      Its slides are theme blocks, and `{% content_for %}` cannot have its output
      captured - theme-check reports it as an error, because Shopify renders
      blocks with their editor bindings attached and buffering that output into a
      variable is not something the platform supports. Handing slides to the shell
      snippet meant capturing them first.

      The shell is not duplicated. `carousel-shell-attrs` writes the element's
      attributes and `carousel-shell-tail` writes the arrows, pagination, pause
      button and live region - the same markup `carousel-shell.liquid` emits, from
      the same sub-snippets. Only the element and its track live here, which is
      the minimum that lets `content_for` sit inside the track.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign cs_layout = section.settings.layout
      assign cs_layout_mobile = layout_mob
      assign cs_label = 'accessibility.carousel' | t

      assign cs_is_carousel = false
      if cs_layout == 'carousel' or cs_layout_mobile == 'carousel'
        assign cs_is_carousel = true
      endif
    -%}

    <swiper-carousel
      {% render 'carousel-shell-attrs',
         settings: section.settings,
         layout: cs_layout,
         layout_mobile: cs_layout_mobile,
         classes: 'multicolumn__carousel',
         columns_desktop: section.settings.columns_desktop,
         columns_tablet: section.settings.columns_tablet,
         columns_mobile: section.settings.columns_mobile %}
    >
      <div
        class="carousel-shell__track multicolumn__grid"
        data-ref="track"
        {% if cs_is_carousel %}aria-label="{{ cs_label | escape }}"{% endif %}
      >
        {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      </div>

      {% render 'carousel-shell-tail',
         settings: section.settings,
         layout: cs_layout,
         layout_mobile: cs_layout_mobile %}
    </swiper-carousel>

  </div>
</div>


